{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>וריב</b> — The commentator says that Judah is faithful and he will be the one who reproves, and he says that Scripture did not say 'a controversy of YHWH against Judah,' but rather with the meaning that HaShem and Judah will contend against Ephraim. But he has erred from the way of the text and grammar. For above he wrote 'and Judah is yet [?, see n] his wound [הוזקו / מזורו]; I will contend against Ephraim, Judah will plow.' And upon both of them he said: 'you have eaten the fruit of lies.' Also ויריבו, 'the shepherds of Gerar strove with the shepherds of Isaac,' and 'the people strove with Moses,' and many others. Therefore he joined Ephraim with Judah and said: 'and to visit upon Jacob according to his ways' — for this name includes both of them."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The commentator's reading of the lemma is unclear; the phrase ארכיב אפרים appears garbled, and the preceding clause (reading מזורו) does not match the standard Masoretic text of Hosea. Translated hyper-literally as the line is possibly corrupt or a paraphrase."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:02.831319179Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}